\description{
\code{load_nba_stats_matchups()} reads the
\verb{leagueseasonmatchups_regular-season_\{per_mode\}_\{END year\}.parquet} files
of the \code{nba_stats_matchups} release: one row per (offensive player,
defensive player) pair. The tag publishes this table for the regular
season only. \code{load_nba_stats_matchups_rollup()} reads the
\verb{matchupsrollup_\{season_type\}_\{per_mode\}_\{END year\}.parquet} files: one
row per defender per offensive position (\code{G}/\code{F}/\code{C}) plus a \code{TOTAL} row.

\code{matchup_min} is \code{"MM:SS"} text in \code{totals} files and decimal minutes in
\code{pergame} files, so reading both per modes makes it character. Pass one
\code{per_mode} to keep the native types. Per-game matchups are in
\code{\link[=load_nba_stats_game_matchups]{load_nba_stats_game_matchups()}}.
}
